.TH OZI 1 "2026" "OziOS" "OziOS commands"
.SH NAME
ozi \- everyday system commands for OziOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ozi
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ozi
is the one command for the things done most often on an OziOS system:
updating, installing, checking and tuning.
Software is reviewed before it is installed; see
.BR ozi\-pkg (1).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B update
Update the system. A snapshot is taken first when snapper is set up.
.TP
.BI install " package..."
Install packages from the repositories or the AUR.
.TP
.BI remove " package..."
Remove packages and the dependencies nothing else needs.
.TP
.BI search " term"
Search for packages.
.TP
.BI review " file"
Check a .deb, an Arch package or an AppImage for known bad patterns before installing it.
.TP
.BI box " file.deb"
Install a Debian or Ubuntu package into its own container.
.TP
.B apps
List the apps installed in boxes.
.TP
.B rollback
List the snapshots the system can be rolled back to.
.TP
.BI layout " name"
Set the panel layout: \fBdefault\fR, \fBdeck\fR, \fBclassic\fR, and \fBboard\fR in the Education edition.
.TP
.B theme \fR[\fIname\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Colours of the whole desktop: \fBcyan\fR (the default), \fBaurora\fR, \fBember\fR, \fBmint\fR,
\fBrose\fR or \fBfrost\fR (light). The bar, the dock, popups, the wallpaper and window frames all
change at once. Without a name it lists the themes and marks the one in use.
.TP
.B theme auto \fR[\fBoff\fR] [\fB\-\-day\fR \fIname\fR] [\fB\-\-night\fR \fIname\fR]
Follow the time of day: the day theme (\fBfrost\fR unless told otherwise) from 07:00 to 19:00, the night
theme the rest of the time, checked every ten minutes by a timer of the user's session.
Picking a theme by hand, or \fBoff\fR, ends it.
.TP
.B look \fR[\fBpreset\fR \fIname\fR | \fIsetting\fR [\fIvalue\fR]] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
How windows look and move. The presets set everything at once: \fBfluid\fR (floating windows with a
glow and blur), \fBtiling\fR (every desktop tiled, no title bars) and \fBlight\fR (no glow or blur, for
older computers). One setting at a time: \fBradius\fR (0 to 24) and \fBoutline\fR (0 to 4) of the window
frames, \fBglow\fR and \fBtitlebar\fR (on or off), \fBgaps\fR between tiles (0 to 40), \fBtiling\fR of
every desktop from the start, \fBblur\fR, and the animation \fBspeed\fR (off, fast, normal, relaxed).
Without arguments it shows them all. The Look app does the same with a preview; Meta+K shows the keys.
.TP
.B quick \fR[\fIsetting\fR [\fIvalue\fR]] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
The quick settings of the control centre in the bar: \fBvolume\fR (a per cent like 40, or +5 and \-5),
\fBmute\fR (on, off or toggle), \fBwifi\fR, \fBbluetooth\fR, \fBnight\fR light and \fBdnd\fR, do not disturb
(on or off). They are read and set with wpctl, nmcli, rfkill, KWin's night light and kde\-inhibit, so
Plasma's own settings show the same. A setting the computer does not have is shown as none.
.TP
.BI effects " level"
Window effects: \fBfull\fR, \fBlight\fR or \fBoff\fR.
.TP
.B mode game on|off
Game mode: performance power profile and no compositing effects while it is on.
.TP
.B status \fR[\fB\-\-json\fR]
Version, kernel, layout, effects, game mode, Windows guest and waiting updates.
.TP
.B doctor \fR[\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-quiet\fR]
Check that the system is in good shape. Exits with status 1 when something needs attention.
.TP
.B report \fR[\fB\-\-output\fR \fIfile\fR] [\fB\-\-stdout\fR]
Write a report for a bug report. Names, addresses and serial numbers are removed first.
Nothing is sent anywhere.
.TP
.B clean \fR[\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-only\fR \fIitems\fR]
Free disk space. Without \fB\-\-yes\fR it only shows what could be freed.
Items: \fBcache\fR, \fBjournal\fR, \fBorphans\fR, \fBuser\fR.
.TP
.B play \fR[\fB\-\-gpu\fR \fIchoice\fR] [\fB\-\-mangohud\fR] \fB\-\-\fR \fIcommand\fR
Run a game with game mode on and put things back afterwards.
In Steam, set the launch options to \fBozi play \-\- %command%\fR.
.TP
.B gaming \fR[\fB\-\-yes\fR]
Install Steam, game mode, MangoHud, Gamescope and the 32\-bit graphics drivers that match the
graphics card in this machine. Without \fB\-\-yes\fR it only lists what is missing.
.TP
.B winsetup
Set up the Windows guest from a Windows ISO.
.TP
.B reboot\-windows
Reboot into a real Windows installed next to OziOS.
.TP
.B hw
Show what this machine supports for the Windows guest.
.TP
.B help
Show a short help text.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/ozios/
The current layout and the game mode flag.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ozi\-pkg (1)
